                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "ellipsis",
                                            "often",
                                            "plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c3a4f79e-64e9-48c2-8b39-f52a415d8416",
                                                "sense_id": "f2bfccec-eb69-3304-a31f-48c5bb19dd7d",
                                                "text": "A hasty and passionate breaker will often make a really goodtempered young horse an inveterate gibber"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3330c503-5d58-4c6f-8e61-066614cd0107",
                                                "sense_id": "f2bfccec-eb69-3304-a31f-48c5bb19dd7d",
                                                "text": "My beauty endures even as I endure; still, if thou wilt, oh rash man, have thy will; but blame not me if passion mount thy reason, as the Egyptian breakers used to mount a colt, and guide it whither thou wilt not."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d6c7aed7-15fd-3529-b672-cf855efc6b7c",
                                        "entry_id": "d14fe171-e164-33c9-80f2-47485a790e38",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A wave breaking into foam against the shore, or against a sandbank, or a rock or reef near the surface, considered a useful warning to ships of an underwater hazard"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "in-plural"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6dd22264-bdda-49a0-87ca-454187447571",
                                                "sense_id": "d6c7aed7-15fd-3529-b672-cf855efc6b7c",
                                                "text": "Now and then in the lagoon you hear the leaping of a fish[…]. And above all, ceaseless like time, is the dull roar of the breakers on the reef."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d7e12ea9-3b33-470d-bee8-563ff5a14dd2",
                                                "sense_id": "d6c7aed7-15fd-3529-b672-cf855efc6b7c",
                                                "text": "And then went down to the ship,\nSet keel to breakers, forth on the godly sea"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84f80131-5eb0-48c1-90c7-32eccbe61477",
                                                "sense_id": "d6c7aed7-15fd-3529-b672-cf855efc6b7c",
                                                "text": "There came a cry \"Oh, there be breakers dead ahead!\" / From the collier Nightingale"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bd12a416-1b39-3840-a51f-a59ca6360ed5",
